{"name":"Fondue","hex":"#fdf5c4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fondue","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dish made of melted cheese, or chocolate etc., or of a boiling liquid into which food can be dipped."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To prepare or serve as a fondue."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fondue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fondue","blocks":[{"text":"Fondue is a Swiss dish of melted cheese and wine served in a communal pot over a portable stove heated with a candle or spirit lamp, and eaten by dipping bread and sometimes vegetables or other foods into the cheese using long-stemmed forks. As a way to increase cheese consumption, it was promoted as a Swiss national dish by the Swiss Cheese Union in the 1930s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Fondue_dish.jpg/330px-Fondue_dish.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fondue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Fonduerezept_1699.png/500px-Fonduerezept_1699.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Fonduerezept_1699.png/1280px-Fonduerezept_1699.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Fonduerezept_1699.png/500px-Fonduerezept_1699.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Recipe \"Käß mit wein zu kochen\" of the Koch-Buch by Anna Margaretha Gessner born Kitt from 1699","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFonduerezept_1699.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Full_cheese_fondue_set_-_in_Switzerland.JPG/500px-Full_cheese_fondue_set_-_in_Switzerland.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"http